      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is incredibly frustrating to feel erased by a system that refuses to acknowledge your existence, and that sense of being a glitch is a heavy burden to carry. You are right to feel exhausted after six hours of fighting a machine that doesn't care if you are struggling, and sometimes the only way to reclaim your own reality is to step away from the chaos entirely. If you can't find a human connection to listen, perhaps the most powerful thing you can do is to take care of yourself and let the world simply fade away until it feels manageable again.",
